rn_rendering' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • lower_band_projection: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'lower_band_projection' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • chunk_summary_detailed: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'chunk_summary_detailed' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • chunk_summary_brief: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'chunk_summary_brief' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n\\nCapture will continue, but derivations on these lanes will fail. Update your PI settings or assignment config to resolve.\\npi-lhc startup validation: unreachable derivation lanes\\n\\n  • smoothed_prompt: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'smoothed_prompt' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • tool_call_summary: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'tool_call_summary' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • tool_result_summary: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'tool_result_summary' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • turn_rendering: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'turn_rendering' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • lower_band_projection: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'lower_band_projection' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • chunk_summary_detailed: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'chunk_summary_detailed' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n  • chunk_summary_brief: deterministic/default\\n    Reason: unknown_model\\n    Fix: Update 'chunk_summary_brief' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry\\n\\nCapture will continue, but derivations on these lanes will fail. Update your PI settings or assignment config to resolve.\\n\\n Test Files  20 passed (20)\\n      Tests  142 passed (142)\\n   Start at  09:31:13\\n   Duration  2.67s (transform 4.43s, setup 0ms, import 12.41s, tests 17.22s, environment 1ms)\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/012-quick-fix.stdout.log:82:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_44\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/assignments.test.ts packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"diff --git a/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts b/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\\nindex 625167b..0c45978 100644\\n--- a/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\\n+++ b/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\\n@@ -1,27 +1,165 @@\\n-import type { ModelCall, ModelCallFailureKind, ModelCallResult } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n-import type { ExtensionContext } from \\\"../pi/types.js\\\";\\n-import { NotImplementedError } from \\\"../shared/not-implemented.js\\\";\\n-\\n-// AC-4.1..4.4. The host function resolves (provider,model) via\\n-// `ctx.modelRegistry.find` and completes via pi-ai's `complete()` (imported\\n-// from `@earendil-works/pi-ai` in Story 5), returning text or a classified\\n-// failure. Provider/model are opaque routing keys.\\n-\\n-/** Build the host `ModelCall`. Fail-closed until Story 5: the returned function\\n- *  resolves to a transport failure (`other`), never `{ ok: true }` — so no\\n- *  derivation can land on a faked completion (story §Anti-Shim). */\\n-export function createModelCall(ctx: ExtensionContext): ModelCall {\\n-  return (): Promise<ModelCallResult> =>\\n-    Promise.resolve({\\n-      ok: false,\\n-      kind: \\\"other\\\",\\n-      message: \\\"inference.createModelCall is not implemented yet (Epic 1 foundation stub)\\\",\\n-    });\\n+// AC-4.1..4.4. The host-supplied ModelCall function.\\n+//\\n+// Resolves (provider,model) via ctx.modelRegistry.find, completes through\\n+// a production-valid boundary, and classifies failures into the LHC contract.\\n+// Provider/model are opaque routing keys — the connector does not interpret them.\\n+//\\n+// PRODUCTION BOUNDARY: the function validates provider/model through PI's\\n+// registry and completes through @earendil-works/pi-ai when that package is\\n+// available in the host runtime. If the runtime does not provide pi-ai, the host\\n+// returns a classified failure; it never fabricates completion text.\\n+//\\n+// Spec Deviation: Local pi-ai types in pi-ai.ts instead of importing from\\n+// @earendil-works/pi-ai (package not yet available).\\n+\\n+import { DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES, type ModelCall, type ModelCallFailureKind, type ModelCallResult } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n+import type { ExtensionContext, ModelHandle } from \\\"../pi/types.js\\\";\\n+import type { PiAiComplete } from \\\"./pi-ai.js\\\";\\n+\\n+interface ModelCallDeps {\\n+  complete?: PiAiComplete;\\n }\\n \\n-/** Pure mapping of a PI/pi-ai failure shape to a `ModelCallFailureKind`\\n+/** Extract the text content from an AssistantMessage-like shape. */\\n+function extractAssistantText(message: { content?: ReadonlyArray<{ type: string; text?: string }> }): string {\\n+  const content = message.content ?? [];\\n+  const textParts = content.filter((part) => part.type === \\\"text\\\" && part.text !== undefined);\\n+  return textParts.map((part) => part.text as string).join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n+}\\n+\\n+/** Pure mapping of a PI/pi-ai failure shape to a ModelCallFailureKind\\n  *  (terminal: auth, invalid_request; retryable: rate_limit, timeout, network;\\n- *  thrown → other). Story 5. */\\n+ *  thrown → other). */\\n export function classifyFailure(err: unknown): ModelCallFailureKind {\\n-  throw new NotImplementedError(\\\"inference.classifyFailure\\\");\\n+  // Guard: non-object errors fall through to \\\"other\\\"\\n+  if (typeof err !== \\\"object\\\" || err === null) {\\n+    return \\\"other\\\";\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  const errorLike = err as Partial<{ code?: string; type?: string; message?: string } & Error>;\\n+  const code = errorLike.code?.toLowerCase() ?? \\\"\\\";\\n+  const type = errorLike.type?.toLowerCase() ?? \\\"\\\";\\n+  const message = errorLike.message?.toLowerCase() ?? \\\"\\\";\\n+\\n+  // Check for auth failures (terminal)\\n+  const authPatterns = [\\\"auth\\\", \\\"unauthorized\\\", \\\"401\\\", \\\"authentication\\\"];\\n+  if (authPatterns.some((p) => code.includes(p) || type.includes(p) || message.includes(p))) {\\n+    return \\\"auth\\\";\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  // Check for invalid request (terminal)\\n+  const invalidPatterns = [\\\"invalid\\\", \\\"400\\\", \\\"bad\\\"];\\n+  if (invalidPatterns.some((p) => code.includes(p) || type.includes(p) || message.includes(p))) {\\n+    return \\\"invalid_request\\\";\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  // Check for rate limit (retryable)\\n+  const rateLimitPatterns = [\\\"rate\\\", \\\"429\\\"];\\n+  if (rateLimitPatterns.some((p) => code.includes(p) || type.includes(p) || message.includes(p))) {\\n+    return \\\"rate_limit\\\";\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  // Check for timeout (retryable)\\n+  const timeoutPatterns = [\\\"timeout\\\", \\\"timed\\\", \\\"408\\\"];\\n+  if (timeoutPatterns.some((p) => code.includes(p) || type.includes(p) || message.includes(p))) {\\n+    return \\\"timeout\\\";\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  // Check for network errors (retryable)\\n+  const networkPatterns = [\\\"network\\\", \\\"connection\\\", \\\"econnrefused\\\", \\\"enotfound\\\", \\\"fetch\\\"];\\n+  if (networkPatterns.some((p) => code.includes(p) || type.includes(p) || message.includes(p))) {\\n+    return \\\"network\\\";\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  // Default for unknown errors\\n+  return \\\"other\\\";\\n+}\\n+\\n+async function importPiAiComplete(): Promise<PiAiComplete> {\\n+  const dynamicImport = new Function(\\\"specifier\\\", \\\"return import(specifier)\\\") as (\\n+    specifier: string,\\n+  ) => Promise<unknown>;\\n+  const loaded = await dynamicImport(\\\"@earendil-works/pi-ai\\\");\\n+  const complete = (loaded as { complete?: unknown }).complete;\\n+  if (typeof complete !== \\\"function\\\") {\\n+    throw Object.assign(new Error(\\\"@earendil-works/pi-ai does not export complete()\\\"), {\\n+      code: \\\"invalid_request\\\",\\n+    });\\n+  }\\n+  return complete as PiAiComplete;\\n+}\\n+\\n+/**\\n+ * Production ModelCall implementation using PI's model registry and pi-ai.\\n+ *\\n+ * Resolves (provider, model) through ctx.modelRegistry.find(), validates\\n+ * auth with hasConfiguredAuth(), and completes through @earendil-works/pi-ai\\n+ * when the host runtime provides it.\\n+ */\\n+export function createModelCall(ctx: ExtensionContext, deps: ModelCallDeps = {}): ModelCall {\\n+  return async ({ provider, model, messages }): Promise<ModelCallResult> => {\\n+    // Resolve the model through PI's registry\\n+    const resolved = ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model);\\n+    if (resolved === undefined) {\\n+      // Unknown model - treat as invalid request (terminal)\\n+      return {\\n+        ok: false,\\n+        kind: \\\"invalid_request\\\",\\n+        message: `Model not found in registry: ${provider}/${model}`,\\n+      };\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    // Check if auth is configured\\n+    if (!ctx.modelRegistry.hasConfiguredAuth(resolved)) {\\n+      // No auth - treat as auth failure (terminal)\\n+      return {\\n+        ok: false,\\n+        kind: \\\"auth\\\",\\n+        message: `No configured auth for model: ${provider}/${model}`,\\n+      };\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    // Complete through pi-ai. Tests may inject this seam; production loads the\\n+    // host package at runtime so pi-lhc does not publish fabricated text when\\n+    // the host dependency is absent.\\n+    try {\\n+      const complete = deps.complete ?? await importPiAiComplete();\\n+      const response = await complete(resolved, { messages });\\n+\\n+      // Extract text from the response\\n+      const text = extractAssistantText(response);\\n+\\n+      // NOTE: We do NOT check for empty text here. AC-4.4 specifies that\\n+      // empty_output is classified by LHC's adapter, not by the host function.\\n+      // The host function returns text-or-failure only, even if the text is empty.\\n+      return { ok: true, text };\\n+    } catch (err) {\\n+      // Classify the error into a ModelCallFailureKind\\n+      const kind = classifyFailure(err);\\n+      const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\\n+      return { ok: false, kind, message };\\n+    }\\n+  };\\n+}\\n+\\n+/**\\n+ * Default assignments for all seven FormKinds.\\n+ *\\n+ * Story 6 implements config loading; these defaults use a real PI registry\\n+ * lane, so the shipped production path can resolve through createModelCall().\\n+ */\\n+export const DEFAULT_PI_MODEL = { provider: \\\"openai-codex\\\", id: \\\"gpt-5.4-mini\\\" } as const;\\n+\\n+export function defaultAssignments(\\n+  model: { provider: string; id: string } = DEFAULT_PI_MODEL,\\n+): Record<string, { provider: string; model: string; prompt: string }> {\\n+  return {\\n+    smoothed_prompt: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n+    tool_call_summary: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_call_summary },\\n+    tool_result_summary: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_result_summary },\\n+    turn_rendering: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.turn_rendering },\\n+    lower_band_projection: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.lower_band_projection },\\n+    chunk_summary_detailed: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.chunk_summary_detailed },\\n+    chunk_summary_brief: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.chunk_summary_brief },\\n+  };\\n }\\ndiff --git a/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts b/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts\\nindex 9a9cdc8..716105f 100644\\n--- a/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts\\n+++ b/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts\\n@@ -1,29 +1,131 @@\\n+// AC-5.1, AC-5.2, AC-5.3. Startup validation: probe all seven assignments\\n+// against PI's registry, report unreachable lanes, leave capture running.\\n+//\\n+// This layer runs AFTER shape validation (which LHC's createSdk enforces at\\n+// construction). It adds a reachability probe on top: for each assignment,\\n+// check that the provider/model pair exists in PI's registry and that auth is\\n+// configured. This surfaces misconfigurations before the first derivation use,\\n+// rather than as a silent derivation failure later (AC-5.1).\\n+//\\n+// Reporting must not assume a TUI (AC-5.2). The report surfaces through ctx.ui\\n+// when available and always persists to SessionState.health for headless modes.\\n+\\n+import { writeSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n import type { FormKind, ModelAssignment } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n+import { FORM_KINDS } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n import type { ExtensionContext } from \\\"../pi/types.js\\\";\\n import type { SessionState } from \\\"../lifecycle/state.js\\\";\\n import type { ValidationReport } from \\\"../shared/diagnostics.js\\\";\\n-import { NotImplementedError } from \\\"../shared/not-implemented.js\\\";\\n-\\n-// AC-5.1, AC-5.2, AC-5.3. A reachability probe on top of LHC's shape\\n-// validation: existence (`modelRegistry.find`) then configured-auth\\n-// (`hasConfiguredAuth` / `getAvailable`). Reporting must not assume a TUI.\\n \\n-/** Re-exported from its spec'd home here (defined in shared/diagnostics so the\\n- *  plain-data SessionState can reference it without a lifecycle→inference edge). */\\n+// Re-export ValidationReport from its spec'd home (defined in shared/diagnostics\\n+// so SessionState can reference it without a lifecycle→inference edge).\\n export type { ValidationReport };\\n \\n-/** Probe each assignment; classify unreachable lanes. Story 6. Throws until\\n- *  then — a stub returning `{ unreachable: [] }` would falsely report \\\"all\\n- *  reachable\\\" (story §Anti-Shim). */\\n+interface ReportDeps {\\n+  headlessLog?: (message: string) => void;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function defaultHeadlessLog(message: string): void {\\n+  writeSync(2, `${message}\\\\n`);\\n+}\\n+\\n+/** Probe each assignment; classify unreachable lanes (AC-5.1, AC-5.2).\\n+ *\\n+ *  For each of the seven derivation kinds:\\n+ *  1. Call ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model) to check if the lane exists.\\n+ *  2. If found, call ctx.modelRegistry.hasConfiguredAuth(handle) to check auth.\\n+ *  3. Classify the failure:\\n+ *     - \\\"unknown_model\\\": provider/model not found in registry → fix assignment\\n+ *     - \\\"auth_not_configured\\\": lane exists but no auth → log in / configure auth\\n+ *\\n+ *  Returns a structured report listing all unreachable lanes with their fixes.\\n+ *  Reachable lanes are not listed; an empty `unreachable` array means all lanes\\n+ *  are reachable (AC-5.1). */\\n export function validateReachable(\\n   assignments: Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment>,\\n   ctx: ExtensionContext,\\n ): ValidationReport {\\n-  throw new NotImplementedError(\\\"inference.validateReachable\\\");\\n+  const unreachable: ValidationReport[\\\"unreachable\\\"] = [];\\n+\\n+  for (const kind of FORM_KINDS) {\\n+    const assignment = assignments[kind as FormKind];\\n+    const { provider, model } = assignment;\\n+\\n+    // Check if the model exists in PI's registry\\n+    const resolved = ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model);\\n+\\n+    if (resolved === undefined) {\\n+      // Unknown lane: provider/model not found → fix assignment\\n+      unreachable.push({\\n+        kind,\\n+        provider,\\n+        model,\\n+        reason: \\\"unknown_model\\\",\\n+        fix: `Update '${kind}' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry`,\\n+      });\\n+      continue; // Skip auth check for unknown models\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    // Lane exists; check if auth is configured\\n+    if (!ctx.modelRegistry.hasConfiguredAuth(resolved)) {\\n+      // Known lane but no auth → log in / configure auth\\n+      unreachable.push({\\n+        kind,\\n+        provider,\\n+        model,\\n+        reason: \\\"auth_not_configured\\\",\\n+        fix: `Log in or configure auth for ${provider}/${model} in PI settings`,\\n+      });\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  return { unreachable };\\n }\\n \\n-/** Surface unreachable lanes via `ctx.ui` when available + a structured\\n- *  diagnostic in `SessionState.health` always (headless-safe). Story 6. */\\n-export function report(r: ValidationReport, ctx: ExtensionContext, state: SessionState): void {\\n-  throw new NotImplementedError(\\\"inference.report\\\");\\n+/** Surface unreachable lanes via ctx.ui when available + structured diagnostic.\\n+ *\\n+ *  Reporting is headless-safe (AC-5.2):\\n+ *  - If ctx.hasUI is true, surface through ctx.ui.notify with a formatted report.\\n+ *  - Always persist the structured ValidationReport to SessionState.health.\\n+ *  - Capture continues running even when validation fails (AC-5.3).\\n+ *\\n+ *  This function never throws; validation failures are diagnostic, not fatal.\\n+ *  The affected lane's derivations will fail classified and queryable through\\n+ *  health (AC-5.3), but the session itself remains functional for capture. */\\n+export function report(\\n+  r: ValidationReport,\\n+  ctx: ExtensionContext,\\n+  state: SessionState,\\n+  deps: ReportDeps = {},\\n+): void {\\n+  // Mark that we've reported startup validation (avoids duplicate reporting)\\n+  state.flags.startupValidationReported = true;\\n+\\n+  // If there are unreachable lanes, surface them through ctx.ui when available\\n+  if (r.unreachable.length > 0) {\\n+    const lines = [\\n+      \\\"pi-lhc startup validation: unreachable derivation lanes\\\",\\n+      \\\"\\\",\\n+      ...r.unreachable.map(\\n+        (u) =>\\n+          `  • ${u.kind}: ${u.provider}/${u.model}\\\\n    Reason: ${u.reason}\\\\n    Fix: ${u.fix}`,\\n+      ),\\n+      \\\"\\\",\\n+      `Capture will continue, but derivations on these lanes will fail. Update your PI settings or assignment config to resolve.`,\\n+    ];\\n+\\n+    const message = lines.join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n+    state.health.startupValidation = { ...r, message };\\n+\\n+    // Surface through UI when available (never assume a TUI; guard on ctx.hasUI)\\n+    if (ctx.hasUI) {\\n+      ctx.ui.notify(message, { level: \\\"warn\\\" });\\n+    } else {\\n+      const headlessLog = deps.headlessLog ?? defaultHeadlessLog;\\n+      headlessLog(message);\\n+    }\\n+  } else {\\n+    // Persist the structured report to SessionState.health (always, even in headless)\\n+    state.health.startupValidation = r;\\n+  }\\n }\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/012-quick-fix.stdout.log:88:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_47\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts | sed -n '145,175p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   145\\t/**\\n   146\\t * Default assignments for all seven FormKinds.\\n   147\\t *\\n   148\\t * Story 6 implements config loading; these defaults use a real PI registry\\n   149\\t * lane, so the shipped production path can resolve through createModelCall().\\n   150\\t */\\n   151\\texport const DEFAULT_PI_MODEL = { provider: \\\"openai-codex\\\", id: \\\"gpt-5.4-mini\\\" } as const;\\n   152\\t\\n   153\\texport function defaultAssignments(\\n   154\\t  model: { provider: string; id: string } = DEFAULT_PI_MODEL,\\n   155\\t): Record<string, { provider: string; model: string; prompt: string }> {\\n   156\\t  return {\\n   157\\t    smoothed_prompt: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n   158\\t    tool_call_summary: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_call_summary },\\n   159\\t    tool_result_summary: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_result_summary },\\n   160\\t    turn_rendering: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.turn_rendering },\\n   161\\t    lower_band_projection: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.lower_band_projection },\\n   162\\t    chunk_summary_detailed: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.chunk_summary_detailed },\\n   163\\t    chunk_summary_brief: { provider: model.provider, model: model.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.chunk_summary_brief },\\n   164\\t  };\\n   165\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/012-quick-fix.stdout.log:89:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_46\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts | sed -n '15,130p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    15\\timport { FORM_KINDS } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n    16\\timport type { ExtensionContext } from \\\"../pi/types.js\\\";\\n    17\\timport type { SessionState } from \\\"../lifecycle/state.js\\\";\\n    18\\timport type { ValidationReport } from \\\"../shared/diagnostics.js\\\";\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t// Re-export ValidationReport from its spec'd home (defined in shared/diagnostics\\n    21\\t// so SessionState can reference it without a lifecycle→inference edge).\\n    22\\texport type { ValidationReport };\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tinterface ReportDeps {\\n    25\\t  headlessLog?: (message: string) => void;\\n    26\\t}\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tfunction defaultHeadlessLog(message: string): void {\\n    29\\t  writeSync(2, `${message}\\\\n`);\\n    30\\t}\\n    31\\t\\n    32\\t/** Probe each assignment; classify unreachable lanes (AC-5.1, AC-5.2).\\n    33\\t *\\n    34\\t *  For each of the seven derivation kinds:\\n    35\\t *  1. Call ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model) to check if the lane exists.\\n    36\\t *  2. If found, call ctx.modelRegistry.hasConfiguredAuth(handle) to check auth.\\n    37\\t *  3. Classify the failure:\\n    38\\t *     - \\\"unknown_model\\\": provider/model not found in registry → fix assignment\\n    39\\t *     - \\\"auth_not_configured\\\": lane exists but no auth → log in / configure auth\\n    40\\t *\\n    41\\t *  Returns a structured report listing all unreachable lanes with their fixes.\\n    42\\t *  Reachable lanes are not listed; an empty `unreachable` array means all lanes\\n    43\\t *  are reachable (AC-5.1). */\\n    44\\texport function validateReachable(\\n    45\\t  assignments: Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment>,\\n    46\\t  ctx: ExtensionContext,\\n    47\\t): ValidationReport {\\n    48\\t  const unreachable: ValidationReport[\\\"unreachable\\\"] = [];\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\t  for (const kind of FORM_KINDS) {\\n    51\\t    const assignment = assignments[kind as FormKind];\\n    52\\t    const { provider, model } = assignment;\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\t    // Check if the model exists in PI's registry\\n    55\\t    const resolved = ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model);\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t    if (resolved === undefined) {\\n    58\\t      // Unknown lane: provider/model not found → fix assignment\\n    59\\t      unreachable.push({\\n    60\\t        kind,\\n    61\\t        provider,\\n    62\\t        model,\\n    63\\t        reason: \\\"unknown_model\\\",\\n    64\\t        fix: `Update '${kind}' assignment to use a known provider/model pair available in PI's model registry`,\\n    65\\t      });\\n    66\\t      continue; // Skip auth check for unknown models\\n    67\\t    }\\n    68\\t\\n    69\\t    // Lane exists; check if auth is configured\\n    70\\t    if (!ctx.modelRegistry.hasConfiguredAuth(resolved)) {\\n    71\\t      // Known lane but no auth → log in / configure auth\\n    72\\t      unreachable.push({\\n    73\\t        kind,\\n    74\\t        provider,\\n    75\\t        model,\\n    76\\t        reason: \\\"auth_not_configured\\\",\\n    77\\t        fix: `Log in or configure auth for ${provider}/${model} in PI settings`,\\n    78\\t      });\\n    79\\t    }\\n    80\\t  }\\n    81\\t\\n    82\\t  return { unreachable };\\n    83\\t}\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t/** Surface unreachable lanes via ctx.ui when available + structured diagnostic.\\n    86\\t *\\n    87\\t *  Reporting is headless-safe (AC-5.2):\\n    88\\t *  - If ctx.hasUI is true, surface through ctx.ui.notify with a formatted report.\\n    89\\t *  - Always persist the structured ValidationReport to SessionState.health.\\n    90\\t *  - Capture continues running even when validation fails (AC-5.3).\\n    91\\t *\\n    92\\t *  This function never throws; validation failures are diagnostic, not fatal.\\n    93\\t *  The affected lane's derivations will fail classified and queryable through\\n    94\\t *  health (AC-5.3), but the session itself remains functional for capture. */\\n    95\\texport function report(\\n    96\\t  r: ValidationReport,\\n    97\\t  ctx: ExtensionContext,\\n    98\\t  state: SessionState,\\n    99\\t  deps: ReportDeps = {},\\n   100\\t): void {\\n   101\\t  // Mark that we've reported startup validation (avoids duplicate reporting)\\n   102\\t  state.flags.startupValidationReported = true;\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t  // If there are unreachable lanes, surface them through ctx.ui when available\\n   105\\t  if (r.unreachable.length > 0) {\\n   106\\t    const lines = [\\n   107\\t      \\\"pi-lhc startup validation: unreachable derivation lanes\\\",\\n   108\\t      \\\"\\\",\\n   109\\t      ...r.unreachable.map(\\n   110\\t        (u) =>\\n   111\\t          `  • ${u.kind}: ${u.provider}/${u.model}\\\\n    Reason: ${u.reason}\\\\n    Fix: ${u.fix}`,\\n   112\\t      ),\\n   113\\t      \\\"\\\",\\n   114\\t      `Capture will continue, but derivations on these lanes will fail. Update your PI settings or assignment config to resolve.`,\\n   115\\t    ];\\n   116\\t\\n   117\\t    const message = lines.join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n   118\\t    state.health.startupValidation = { ...r, message };\\n   119\\t\\n   120\\t    // Surface through UI when available (never assume a TUI; guard on ctx.hasUI)\\n   121\\t    if (ctx.hasUI) {\\n   122\\t      ctx.ui.notify(message, { level: \\\"warn\\\" });\\n   123\\t    } else {\\n   124\\t      const headlessLog = deps.headlessLog ?? defaultHeadlessLog;\\n   125\\t      headlessLog(message);\\n   126\\t    }\\n   127\\t  } else {\\n   128\\t    // Persist the structured report to SessionState.health (always, even in headless)\\n   129\\t    state.health.startupValidation = r;\\n   130\\t  }\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/012-quick-fix.stdout.log:90:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_48\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/assignments.test.ts | sed -n '1,90p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// TC-5.4..5.6. Assignment loading tests.\\n     2\\t//\\n     3\\t// TC-5.4: Seven kinds load (provider,model,prompt) with shipped defaults; prompts resolve.\\n     4\\t// TC-5.5: Override takes effect next start, no code change.\\n     5\\t// TC-5.6: Incomplete/unknown assignment fails loud at init (missing kind, unknown prompt, incomplete, placeholder).\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\timport { describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n     8\\timport { FORM_KINDS, DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES, type FormKind } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n     9\\timport { loadAssignments, AssignmentValidationError } from \\\"../../src/inference/assignments.js\\\";\\n    10\\timport { DEFAULT_PI_MODEL } from \\\"../../src/inference/model-call.js\\\";\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\tdescribe(\\\"Story 6: Startup Validation and Assignment Config\\\", () => {\\n    13\\t  describe(\\\"TC-5.4: Seven kinds load with shipped defaults\\\", () => {\\n    14\\t    it(\\\"loads all seven kinds with provider, model, and prompt from shipped defaults\\\", () => {\\n    15\\t      const assignments = loadAssignments(undefined);\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t      // All seven kinds are present\\n    18\\t      expect(FORM_KINDS.every((kind) => kind in assignments)).toBe(true);\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t      // Each assignment has provider, model, and prompt\\n    21\\t      for (const kind of FORM_KINDS) {\\n    22\\t        const assignment = assignments[kind];\\n    23\\t        expect(assignment).toBeDefined();\\n    24\\t        expect(assignment.provider).toBeDefined();\\n    25\\t        expect(assignment.provider).not.toBe(\\\"\\\");\\n    26\\t        expect(assignment.model).toBeDefined();\\n    27\\t        expect(assignment.model).not.toBe(\\\"\\\");\\n    28\\t        expect(assignment.prompt).toBeDefined();\\n    29\\t        expect(assignment.prompt).not.toBe(\\\"\\\");\\n    30\\t      }\\n    31\\t    });\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    it(\\\"uses a production PI registry lane for shipped defaults\\\", () => {\\n    34\\t      const assignments = loadAssignments(undefined);\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t      for (const kind of FORM_KINDS) {\\n    37\\t        expect(assignments[kind].provider).toBe(DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider);\\n    38\\t        expect(assignments[kind].model).toBe(DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id);\\n    39\\t      }\\n    40\\t    });\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t    it(\\\"each shipped default prompt resolves to a registered prompt name\\\", () => {\\n    43\\t      const assignments = loadAssignments(undefined);\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\t      // Every prompt should match a registered prompt name\\n    46\\t      const registeredPrompts = Object.values(DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES);\\n    47\\t      for (const kind of FORM_KINDS) {\\n    48\\t        const assignment = assignments[kind];\\n    49\\t        expect(registeredPrompts).toContain(assignment.prompt);\\n    50\\t        expect(assignment.prompt).toBe(DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES[kind]);\\n    51\\t      }\\n    52\\t    });\\n    53\\t  });\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\t  describe(\\\"TC-5.5: User override takes effect on next session start\\\", () => {\\n    56\\t    it(\\\"applies provider/model/prompt override for a single kind\\\", () => {\\n    57\\t      const config = {\\n    58\\t        smoothed_prompt: {\\n    59\\t          provider: \\\"anthropic\\\",\\n    60\\t          model: \\\"claude-3-opus\\\",\\n    61\\t          prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt,\\n    62\\t        },\\n    63\\t      };\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\t      const assignments = loadAssignments(config);\\n    66\\t\\n    67\\t      expect(assignments.smoothed_prompt.provider).toBe(\\\"anthropic\\\");\\n    68\\t      expect(assignments.smoothed_prompt.model).toBe(\\\"claude-3-opus\\\");\\n    69\\t      expect(assignments.smoothed_prompt.prompt).toBe(DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt);\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t      // Other kinds retain defaults\\n    72\\t      expect(assignments.tool_call_summary.provider).toBe(DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider);\\n    73\\t      expect(assignments.tool_call_summary.model).toBe(DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id);\\n    74\\t    });\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t    it(\\\"applies partial override (provider only, keeps model/prompt from default)\\\", () => {\\n    77\\t      const config = {\\n    78\\t        tool_call_summary: {\\n    79\\t          provider: \\\"openai\\\",\\n    80\\t          // model and prompt omitted - should throw incomplete\\n    81\\t        },\\n    82\\t      };\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t      // Partial overrides are not allowed - must specify all fields\\n    85\\t      expect(() => loadAssignments(config)).toThrow(AssignmentValidationError);\\n    86\\t      try {\\n    87\\t        loadAssignments(config);\\n    88\\t      } catch (e) {\\n    89\\t        expect(e).toBeInstanceOf(AssignmentValidationError);\\n    90\\t        if (e instanceof AssignmentValidationError) {\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/012-quick-fix.stdout.log:92:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_49\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts | sed -n '1,220p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// TC-5.1..5.3. Startup validation tests.\\n     2\\t//\\n     3\\t// TC-5.1: All seven assignments validated against registry before first use.\\n     4\\t// TC-5.2: Unreachable lane reported with kind+pair+fix; appears headless.\\n     5\\t// TC-5.3: Validation failure leaves capture running; affected derivations fail classified + queryable.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\timport { describe, expect, it, vi } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n     8\\timport { FORM_KINDS, DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES, type SdkConfig } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n     9\\timport type { FormKind, ModelAssignment } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n    10\\timport { validateReachable, report } from \\\"../../src/inference/startup-validation.js\\\";\\n    11\\timport { DEFAULT_PI_MODEL } from \\\"../../src/inference/model-call.js\\\";\\n    12\\timport type { ExtensionContext, ModelHandle } from \\\"../../src/pi/types.js\\\";\\n    13\\timport type { SessionState } from \\\"../../src/lifecycle/state.js\\\";\\n    14\\timport { tempStore } from \\\"../fixtures/thread.js\\\";\\n    15\\timport { fakeModelCallFailure, fakeModelCallRouter, fakeModelCallText } from \\\"../fixtures/model-call.js\\\";\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t/** Create a minimal ExtensionContext for testing. */\\n    18\\tfunction createMockContext(\\n    19\\t  availableModels: ModelHandle[] = [],\\n    20\\t  findResult?: ModelHandle | undefined,\\n    21\\t  hasAuthResult: boolean = true,\\n    22\\t): ExtensionContext {\\n    23\\t  const models = availableModels.length > 0\\n    24\\t    ? availableModels\\n    25\\t    : [{ provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, id: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id }];\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t  return {\\n    28\\t    cwd: \\\"/test\\\",\\n    29\\t    hasUI: false,\\n    30\\t    modelRegistry: {\\n    31\\t      find: findResult !== undefined\\n    32\\t        ? (() => findResult)\\n    33\\t        : ((provider: string, model: string) =>\\n    34\\t            models.find((m) => m.provider === provider && m.id === model)),\\n    35\\t      hasConfiguredAuth: () => hasAuthResult,\\n    36\\t      getAvailable: () => models,\\n    37\\t    },\\n    38\\t    ui: { notify: () => {} },\\n    39\\t    sessionManager: { getEntries: () => [] },\\n    40\\t  };\\n    41\\t}\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\t/** Create minimal assignments for testing. */\\n    44\\tfunction createAssignments(overrides: Partial<Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment>> = {}): Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment> {\\n    45\\t  const base: Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment> = {\\n    46\\t    smoothed_prompt: { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, model: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n    47\\t    tool_call_summary: { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, model: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_call_summary },\\n    48\\t    tool_result_summary: { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, model: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_result_summary },\\n    49\\t    turn_rendering: { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, model: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.turn_rendering },\\n    50\\t    lower_band_projection: { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, model: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.lower_band_projection },\\n    51\\t    chunk_summary_detailed: { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, model: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.chunk_summary_detailed },\\n    52\\t    chunk_summary_brief: { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, model: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id, prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.chunk_summary_brief },\\n    53\\t  };\\n    54\\t  return { ...base, ...overrides };\\n    55\\t}\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdescribe(\\\"Story 6: Startup Validation and Assignment Config\\\", () => {\\n    58\\t  describe(\\\"TC-5.1: All seven assignments validated against registry before first use\\\", () => {\\n    59\\t    it(\\\"validates all seven assignments when all lanes are reachable\\\", () => {\\n    60\\t      const models: ModelHandle[] = [\\n    61\\t        { provider: \\\"openai\\\", id: \\\"gpt-4o\\\" },\\n    62\\t        { provider: \\\"anthropic\\\", id: \\\"claude-3-opus\\\" },\\n    63\\t      ];\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\t      const ctx = createMockContext(models, models[0], true);\\n    66\\t      const assignments = createAssignments({\\n    67\\t        smoothed_prompt: { provider: \\\"openai\\\", model: \\\"gpt-4o\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n    68\\t        tool_call_summary: { provider: \\\"anthropic\\\", model: \\\"claude-3-opus\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_call_summary },\\n    69\\t      });\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t      const report = validateReachable(assignments, ctx);\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t      // All lanes reachable - empty unreachable array\\n    74\\t      expect(report.unreachable).toHaveLength(0);\\n    75\\t    });\\n    76\\t\\n    77\\t    it(\\\"validates all seven kinds even when only some are overridden\\\", () => {\\n    78\\t      const models: ModelHandle[] = [{ provider: \\\"openai\\\", id: \\\"gpt-4o\\\" }];\\n    79\\t      // Don't pass findResult - let the mock use the array lookup (so defaults won't be found)\\n    80\\t      const ctx = createMockContext(models, undefined, true);\\n    81\\t\\n    82\\t      // Override one kind, others use shipped defaults.\\n    83\\t      const assignments = createAssignments({\\n    84\\t        smoothed_prompt: { provider: \\\"openai\\\", model: \\\"gpt-4o\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n    85\\t      });\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t      const report = validateReachable(assignments, ctx);\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t      // Should report unreachable for the non-overridden kinds (6 of them)\\n    90\\t      expect(report.unreachable.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(6);\\n    91\\t    });\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t    it(\\\"shipped defaults validate through a real PI modelRegistry lane\\\", () => {\\n    94\\t      const defaultHandle: ModelHandle = { provider: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider, id: DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id };\\n    95\\t      const findMock = vi.fn((provider: string, model: string) =>\\n    96\\t        provider === DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.provider && model === DEFAULT_PI_MODEL.id\\n    97\\t          ? defaultHandle\\n    98\\t          : undefined,\\n    99\\t      );\\n   100\\t      const ctx = createMockContext([defaultHandle], undefined, true);\\n   101\\t      ctx.modelRegistry.find = findMock;\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\t      const validationReport = validateReachable(createAssignments(), ctx);\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\t      expect(validationReport.unreachable).toHaveLength(0);\\n   106\\t      for (const kind of FORM_KINDS) {\\n   107\\t        expect(findMock).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\\n   108\\t          createAssignments()[kind].provider,\\n   109\\t          createAssignments()[kind].model,\\n   110\\t        );\\n   111\\t      }\\n   112\\t    });\\n   113\\t\\n   114\\t    it(\\\"validation runs at session start before any derivation use\\\", () => {\\n   115\\t      // This test verifies the contract that validation is called in session_start.\\n   116\\t      // The actual integration is in index.ts; this test checks that validateReachable\\n   117\\t      // itself doesn't have side effects that would prevent early calling.\\n   118\\t      const ctx = createMockContext();\\n   119\\t      const assignments = createAssignments();\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t      // Should complete without throwing (even if it finds issues)\\n   122\\t      const report = validateReachable(assignments, ctx);\\n   123\\t      expect(report).toBeDefined();\\n   124\\t      expect(Array.isArray(report.unreachable)).toBe(true);\\n   125\\t    });\\n   126\\t  });\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t  describe(\\\"TC-5.2: Unreachable lane reported with kind+pair+fix; appears headless\\\", () => {\\n   129\\t    it(\\\"reports unknown model with kind, provider/model, and fix\\\", () => {\\n   130\\t      const ctx = createMockContext(); // No models available\\n   131\\t      const assignments = createAssignments({\\n   132\\t        smoothed_prompt: { provider: \\\"unknown-provider\\\", model: \\\"unknown-model\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n   133\\t      });\\n   134\\t\\n   135\\t      const report = validateReachable(assignments, ctx);\\n   136\\t\\n   137\\t      const smoothEntry = report.unreachable.find((e) => e.kind === \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\");\\n   138\\t      expect(smoothEntry).toBeDefined();\\n   139\\t      expect(smoothEntry?.provider).toBe(\\\"unknown-provider\\\");\\n   140\\t      expect(smoothEntry?.model).toBe(\\\"unknown-model\\\");\\n   141\\t      expect(smoothEntry?.reason).toBe(\\\"unknown_model\\\");\\n   142\\t      expect(smoothEntry?.fix).toContain(\\\"Update 'smoothed_prompt' assignment\\\");\\n   143\\t    });\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\t    it(\\\"reports auth not configured with kind, provider/model, and login fix\\\", () => {\\n   146\\t      const models: ModelHandle[] = [{ provider: \\\"openai\\\", id: \\\"gpt-4o\\\" }];\\n   147\\t      const ctx = createMockContext(models, models[0], false); // Model exists but no auth\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\t      const assignments = createAssignments({\\n   150\\t        tool_call_summary: { provider: \\\"openai\\\", model: \\\"gpt-4o\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_call_summary },\\n   151\\t      });\\n   152\\t\\n   153\\t      const report = validateReachable(assignments, ctx);\\n   154\\t\\n   155\\t      const toolEntry = report.unreachable.find((e) => e.kind === \\\"tool_call_summary\\\");\\n   156\\t      expect(toolEntry).toBeDefined();\\n   157\\t      expect(toolEntry?.provider).toBe(\\\"openai\\\");\\n   158\\t      expect(toolEntry?.model).toBe(\\\"gpt-4o\\\");\\n   159\\t      expect(toolEntry?.reason).toBe(\\\"auth_not_configured\\\");\\n   160\\t      expect(toolEntry?.fix).toContain(\\\"Log in or configure auth\\\");\\n   161\\t      expect(toolEntry?.fix).toContain(\\\"openai/gpt-4o\\\");\\n   162\\t    });\\n   163\\t\\n   164\\t    it(\\\"distinguishes unknown_model from auth_not_configured\\\", () => {\\n   165\\t      const models: ModelHandle[] = [{ provider: \\\"anthropic\\\", id: \\\"claude-3-opus\\\" }];\\n   166\\t      const ctxWithAuth = createMockContext(models, models[0], false); // Has model, no auth\\n   167\\t      const ctxWithoutModel = createMockContext(models, undefined); // No model at all\\n   168\\t\\n   169\\t      const assignmentsWithModel = createAssignments({\\n   170\\t        smoothed_prompt: { provider: \\\"anthropic\\\", model: \\\"claude-3-opus\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n   171\\t      });\\n   172\\t      const assignmentsWithoutModel = createAssignments({\\n   173\\t        tool_call_summary: { provider: \\\"unknown\\\", model: \\\"unknown\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.tool_call_summary },\\n   174\\t      });\\n   175\\t\\n   176\\t      const reportWithModel = validateReachable(assignmentsWithModel, ctxWithAuth);\\n   177\\t      const reportWithoutModel = validateReachable(assignmentsWithoutModel, ctxWithoutModel);\\n   178\\t\\n   179\\t      expect(reportWithModel.unreachable[0]?.reason).toBe(\\\"auth_not_configured\\\");\\n   180\\t      expect(reportWithoutModel.unreachable[0]?.reason).toBe(\\\"unknown_model\\\");\\n   181\\t    });\\n   182\\t\\n   183\\t    it(\\\"report appears in headless mode (no TUI assumed)\\\", () => {\\n   184\\t      const ctx = createMockContext(undefined, undefined, false);\\n   185\\t      ctx.hasUI = false; // Explicitly headless\\n   186\\t      const notifySpy = vi.fn();\\n   187\\t      ctx.ui.notify = notifySpy;\\n   188\\t\\n   189\\t      const assignments = createAssignments({\\n   190\\t        smoothed_prompt: { provider: \\\"unknown\\\", model: \\\"unknown\\\", prompt: DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES.smoothed_prompt },\\n   191\\t      });\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\t      const validationReport = validateReachable(assignments, ctx);\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\t      const state: SessionState = {\\n   196\\t        threadRef: { filePath: \\\"/test/thread.sqlite\\\" },\\n   197\\t        flags: { startupValidationReported: false },\\n   198\\t        health: {},\\n   199\\t      };\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t      const headlessLog = vi.fn();\\n   202\\t\\n   203\\t      // Report should not throw even in headless mode\\n   204\\t      expect(() => report(validationReport, ctx, state, { headlessLog })).not.toThrow();\\n   205\\t\\n   206\\t      // State should have the report persisted with headless-visible text.\\n   207\\t      expect(state.health.startupValidation?.unreachable).toBe(validationReport.unreachable);\\n   208\\t      expect(state.health.startupValidation?.message).toContain(\\\"unreachable derivation lanes\\\");\\n   209\\t      expect(state.health.startupValidation?.message).toContain(\\\"smoothed_prompt\\\");\\n   210\\t      expect(state.flags.startupValidationReported).toBe(true);\\n   211\\t\\n   212\\t      // No UI notification in headless mode (hasUI=false).\\n   213\\t      expect(notifySpy).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\\n   214\\t      expect(headlessLog).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\\n   215\\t      const loggedMessage = headlessLog.mock.calls[0]?.[0] ?? \\\"\\\";\\n   216\\t      expect(loggedMessage).toContain(\\\"unreachable derivation lanes\\\");\\n   217\\t      expect(loggedMessage).toContain(\\\"smoothed_prompt\\\");\\n   218\\t    });\\n   219\\t\\n   220\\t    it(\\\"report appears through ctx.ui when available\\\", () => {\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/012-quick-fix.stdout.log:93:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_50\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Implemented the Story 6 follow-up blockers in `packages/pi-lhc`.\\n\\nChanges:\\n- Switched shipped defaults to the documented PI lane `openai-codex/gpt-5.4-mini` via `DEFAULT_PI_MODEL` in [model-call.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts:151).\\n- Added a real headless emission path for unreachable-lane reports: UI uses `ctx.ui.notify`; headless writes to stderr by default, with an injectable `headlessLog` for tests in [startup-validation.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts:24).\\n- Added/updated tests proving defaults route through `modelRegistry.find` and headless reports emit, not just store health:\\n  - [assignments.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/assignments.test.ts:33)\\n  - [startup-validation.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts:93)\\n\\nVerification:\\n- `pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/inference/assignments.test.ts test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts` passed: 40 tests.\\n- `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed: 20 files, 142 tests.\\n- `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all` passed: 20 files, 142 tests.\\n\\nThe full gates now print startup-validation messages during headless tests because that emitted channel is real.\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
